  "summary": "Provide initial treatment as below and refer woman and contacts to GUM service. Always test for gonorrhoea and chlamydia. Appropriate analgesia should be provided. If the risk of gonococcal PID is high (e.g. when the patient's partner has gonorrhoea, in clinically severe disease, following sexual contact abroad), refer such cases directly to GUM for appropriate susceptibility testing, resistance monitoring and treatment.",
